ct that  has been about sizing market  opportunities in different countries so  your client or maybe your team need  asked you to analyze different  geographies and understand if there's a  country where it might make sense for  your company to enter the market with a  certain product that you as a company  are offering so if your communique  focuses a lot on process this means that  you focus a lot on the different steps  that you took to get to a certain  results you're talking all about what  you actually did in the last days in the  last weeks in the last months so an  example could be something like this to  say well I talked to the colleague in  the finance department and then I got  some numbers there and then I put some  market reports to actually combine the  data and then I also looked into  macroeconomic information about the  different countries and then I combined  these things but then I realized that  actually I'm missing certain information  so I went to the marketing department  head and then I talked to her to  understand her opinion about these  geographies and then again our compiled  it and then we had some alignment  meetings with other people of the  organization and then on looking at all  of this this is the result that we came  up with right so this is a process  oriented way of communicating and it  focuses a lot on the things that you did  in order to get through a certain reside  and many people like to talk about the  process this is something that many  people somehow naturally tend to to talk  about the process and probably due to  the fact that it really underlines what  all the effort is that you put into  something it underlines that you really  spend lots of time on a certain task it  underlines that you really worked a lot  that there were just many many things  that you did and you really made a big  and significant effort to solve this  problem but I hope that you also see the  downsides of talking about things in  this way because the focus is on the  steps that you took but the focus is not  on resides and I'll try to put yourself  into the shoes of a CEO of a large blue  chip company and you can assume that he  assumes that usually the people he works  with our professionals and that they  will make sure that the things they  present to him meet a certain level of  quality and  analytical rigor and the truth is to see  or such a company just will not care  about all the meetings that you had all  the time that you put into something all  the analysis that you took and they  maybe found although this actually  didn't work so that then you needed to  look it to something else and this that  maybe worked or not  the CEO will not care okay it does not  care about all the sweat or the work all  of the hours you put into something what  he cares about is the recite and if you  talk so much about the process you will  just waste this time and this is  something you should be very cautious  about to not erase the time of your  co-workers especially or if your parade  in such a professional environment so  this is now the process oriented way of  talking about something let's now look  into the content oriented way how would  you phrase an answer to the question  what you did on a project in a way that  actually focuses much more on the  content but not so much on the process  and talking about content basically  means talking about the results so let  me give you an example what would that  mean to talk about results so if you  talk about the content you could tell  your CEO or something like so from the  analysis that we did so far we conclude  that France like this the country where  for us it would make more sense to enter  with this new product that we have and  for three reasons first consumer  research shows that this product really  meets the needs of French consumers in a  way that it is not the same with the  consumer behavior patterns that we see  in other countries the second reason is  that the competitive situation in these  countries is that currently there is no  strong competitor there offering a  similar product so if we go there now we  have an advantage because we are the  first we can now quickly grow in market  share before maybe others then join the  market later the third reason is that  our operations are very well set up to  enter the French market because we have  warehouses we have a supply chain setup  that is very effective in serving the  French market at the moment it is much  better suited for the French market then  compared to other markets which you  might be so  instead so now let's make a cut to you  this is just an example of how you could  phrase such that no much more focuses on  the content of course not the arguments  that I said we're a habit rarely and  depend on the specific situation that  you're in but hope that you see the  difference that what I did not do is  explaining what all the steps were what  all the data is that I analyzed what the  meetings were that I had what maybe  first I thought but then I needed to  revise because I found out that it  doesn't make sense and something entity  makes much more sense all of the things  I did not talk about what I did talk  about is what the reside us and what the  key arguments are that actually back up  this recite now ask yourself what would  be beyond so that the CEO likely would  be much more interested in and for my  experience in working for several years  of consulting I can tell you that  letters the proper answer to given these  situations letter answer is an answer  that somebody communicates  professionally and effectively we give  so talking about the content is really  the way to go I cannot stress this  enough communications so crucial in any  professional environment and focusing on  content instead of process we're talking  about things that you did when giving  status updates we're talking about your  projects we're talking about the things  that you're working on is really crucial  and distinguishes you as a professional  communicator and of course now I talked  a lot about consulting examples I talked  a lot about the consulting context but  the truth is that this type of  communication behavior is relevant to  pretty much any job that you have it  really does not depend at all in which  industry you're in making sure that you  focus on professional communication is  absolutely key what you'll notice even  when you work in large bhutesu companies  that a lot of people really struggle  with good and effective communication  even senior leaders of some of these  companies really struggle with effective  communication this is something where  you can actually improve very quickly  and make a difference and just shine in  contrast to all these other people and  the key phrase that just summarizes this  kind of communication patterns if you're  looking for a name for all of this to do  further research  it's called top-down communique  she top-down communications the holy  grail in professional communication and  what I just talked about the distinction  between process and content it's just  one aspect of it there are many other  aspects in top-down communication so I'd  like to hear from you I'm interested to  learn more about what professional  communications are about let me know and  I might cover other aspects of this type  of communication in future videos just  as the quick tip if you just want to get  started right away the Bible of this  top-down communication approach is a  book that is called the pyramid  principle by Barbara Minto  it's a book that at least at McKinsey  almost every consultant reads and some  training programs you even get it as a  gift or something you're supposed to  read a lot or advance and I can highly  communicate this book I will even link  to this book in the description below so  if you're interested just check it out  so let me know if you would like to see  more videos on effective communication  in this channel so if you took any value  out of this video at all please press  the like button and subscribe and also  press the notification there to keep up  to date with my channels content I will  release at least one video every week  often even to videos so subscribe to  stay posted I will bring you lots of  content on how to be successful in the  first years in your career drawn from my  experience at McKinsey they're not also  working in a senior leadership position  in a German retailer let me know if you  have any questions in the comments I  will do my very best to give an answer  to every single comment that you write  so hope you're all doing well and had a  good time  stay safe keep learning and thank you  for watching this is highly for firm  learning

